From 688750e3c6fa0c462ab21009c4f0775f7a53b994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:55:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/70] demux: ogg: allow seeking once the streams have been
 torn down

At the end of a stream Demux() tears the logical streams down, parking the
last one in p_old_stream so Ogg_BeginningOfStream() can reuse its ES.
p_sys->i_streams is zero from then on, so Ogg_GetSelectedStream() returns
NULL and every seek is refused.

Seeking out of that state is meaningful: the input seeks back to the start
to repeat a file, and a user can drag the seek bar after the end. Neither
works, and MainLoopTryRepeat() spends the repeat counter as fast as it can.

The parked stream still carries the granule state the seek needs, so fall
back to it: with the read position moved, the next Demux() starts over.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/ogg.c    | 7 +++++++
 src/audio_output/dec.c | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/ogg.c b/modules/demux/ogg.c
index 43b0ebf046..126581eeef 100644
--- a/modules/demux/ogg.c
+++ b/modules/demux/ogg.c
@@ -759,6 +759,13 @@ static logical_stream_t * Ogg_GetSelectedStream( demux_t *p_demux )
             break;
         }
     }
+
+    /* At end of stream the logical streams are torn down and the last one
+     * is parked in p_old_stream; it still has what the seek needs. */
+    if( p_stream == NULL && p_sys->p_old_stream != NULL &&
+        p_sys->p_old_stream->p_es != NULL )
+        p_stream = p_sys->p_old_stream;
+
     return p_stream;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/audio_output/dec.c b/src/audio_output/dec.c
index 7eca0de2fd..b791f81be9 100644
--- a/src/audio_output/dec.c
+++ b/src/audio_output/dec.c
@@ -263,8 +263,9 @@ static void aout_DecSynchronize (audio_output_t *aout, vlc_tick_t dec_pts,
      * This can happen due to insufficient caching, scheduling jitter
      * or bug in the decoder. Ideally, the output would seek backward. But that
      * is not portable, not supported by some hardware and often unsafe/buggy
-     * where supported. The other alternative is to flush the buffers
-     * completely. */
+     * where supported. Play out what is queued and drop as much from what
+     * follows instead: flushing would throw away a second or more of audio,
+     * heard as a hole. */
     if (drift > (owner->sync.discontinuity ? 0
                   : +3 * input_rate * AOUT_MAX_PTS_DELAY / INPUT_RATE_DEFAULT))
     {
